# examples/spec/consensus.cml: the shared base for the consensus family
# (Paxos, Raft, Humming Consensus, ZAB).  It fixes the vocabulary and the
# one safety property they all owe -- Agreement: at most one value is
# ever chosen.  A protocol module `extends consensus`, adds its own
# variables and actions that drive `chosen`, and inherits Agreement
# unchanged, so the category's common requirement is modelled once.
#
# The base itself declares the agreed-value record `chosen` (a function
# from a value to 1 if that value has been chosen, 0 otherwise) and the
# Agreement invariant over it.  A protocol sets chosen[v] = 1 when its
# own rule decides v.

module consensus

const V = 2                     # candidate values are 1 .. V (0 = none)

# chosen[v] = 1 once value v is decided by the protocol
var chosen : [1 .. V -> 0 .. 1]

init chosen == [v in 1 .. V -> 0]

# Agreement: never are two different values both chosen.
invariant agreement: (count v in 1 .. V : chosen[v] == 1) <= 1
